x86_64-linux  the difference is the implicit constructors and destructors, not the RTTI: this case names nine classes and cxx1 emits _ZN4LeafC1Ev and its kind as ordinary definitions where clang emits them linkonce_odr in a comdat, which the collector does not see. The type_info objects themselves - _ZTI and _ZTS for every class here, including the two in a namespace - agree exactly, which is what this case was added to check. The implicit-member difference is older than this case and is not about dynamic_cast; vtable.cpp and virtual.cpp check the same names on classes few enough not to trip it.
arm64-darwin  the same difference, and for the same reason.
